Change(genesis='66602cd0dec37d58d03eec9518ca805a7ac38ea912d2b0c366a0b67b4b9f50b6', deps=('ffd32363c86c63ce9c409c3565c8de14e484b97cb416681787f37d10a82bd486',), event=Revised(decision='gatehalves', at=datetime(2026, 11, 22, 2, 32, 45, 674174), actor='assistant', title="The merge gate has three halves: the tree's, the live one, and what the commit messages declare", body="It has THREE HALVES (2026-10-03; 2026-11-22), each step in exactly one: `--no-live` is the tree half, a function of the tree alone, run with the data tree hidden (`SUZATARY_INSTANCE` names nothing), so it runs on core's runners from the train commit's public tree (`train`); `--only-live` is the live half, on the box only: the steps that read the owner's data tree (`--test live`, the `all` modules in `live_modules`, the guards that read beyond the public tree, `web-live`) and the deploy's checks; `--only-history` is what the commit messages since the merge base declare (`scripts/context.sh growth`, which compiles nothing), and the train runs that same check in its tool before its halves, as a refusal that writes no row. `--list` names every step's half and what it reads beside the tree (`nothing`, or any of `stores`, `history`, `runners`); only `changelog`, unkept, reads the history in the tree half; and `app/cli/tests/guards/merge_gate.rs` fails when a test that reads the data tree is outside the live half, or a step reads what its half does not.", rationale="Decided 2026-10-03. Restated 2026-11-20: the tree half runs on core's runners, and the Codespace it ran in is gone. Restated 2026-11-22: a verdict is of what it read (the live row's digest, the set-aside, the growth check before the halves).", supersedes=()))